  Headline and caption say the expired powder was 'sold', and the caption says the supermarket 'failed to respond' after being asked; the article says the powder was sold after its expiry date, which matches, but the reel_script's phrase 'அதில்... மூலிகை பொடி பாக்கெட்டின் விலை 10 ரூபாய்' is fine; however the slide and caption wording 'காலாவதி தேதி முடிந்து ஒரு மாதத்திற்கு பிறகும் அந்தப் பொடி விற்கப்பட்டது' conflates two facts: the article says the purchase/sale happened after the expiry date plus one month, which the draft states as sold one month after expiry, a slight mismatch with the article's wording.
  The reel_script says the packet was checked at home and 'அது விற்கப்பட்டது தெரியவந்தது' but the article states the discovery was that it was sold after expiry; the reel_script omits that the buyer went to the supermarket and asked, which is present, so no omission there.
  The reel_script and caption say 'பெற்ற தொகை 10 ரூபாயைத் திருப்பிச் செலுத்த வேண்டும்' — accurate; but the headline 'ரூ.10 திருப்பித் தர உத்தரவு' omits the 5,000 ரூபாய compensation and litigation cost, which is an important part of the order and is missing from the headline (though present in the reel and slides).
  The slide 'புகார் என்ன ஆனது?' line 'கவுண்டம்பாளையம், கே.கே.புதூர் ரோட்டைச் சேர்ந்த சண்முக' is cut off mid-name and truncates the buyer's name, an incomplete and unclear Tamil line.
